Template: otzi-headless/role
Type: select
Choices: leader, leaf
Default: leaf
Description: Node role for bootstrap
 During the initial setup phase, one node hosts a bootstrap server
 (the "leader") and the others connect to it (the "leaves") to exchange
 long-term identity public keys. This choice only affects the bootstrap
 step (`otzi setup`). After bootstrap, all nodes are peers in the
 threshold ceremony.

Template: otzi-headless/network
Type: select
Choices: mainnet, testnet, regtest
Default: testnet
Description: Bitcoin network

Template: otzi-headless/opnet-rpc
Type: string
Description: OPNet RPC URL
 Operator-side broadcast paths (and any future read endpoints) default
 to this URL. Per-network defaults: https://api.opnet.org (mainnet),
 https://testnet.opnet.org (testnet), http://127.0.0.1:9001 (regtest).

Template: otzi-headless/peer-hostnames
Type: string
Description: Peer hostnames (space-separated, optional)
 List the hostnames or IPs of the other nodes in the ring (e.g.
 "node-b.example node-c.example"). Used to populate stub [[peers]]
 entries in the generated daemon.toml. Leave blank to fill in manually
 after bootstrap. The bootstrap step (`otzi setup`) discovers each
 peer's identity pubkey + party_id; you complete the [[peers]] block
 by editing /etc/otzi/daemon.toml.

Template: otzi-headless/transport
Type: select
Choices: peer-mesh, relay
Default: peer-mesh
Description: Transport kind
 "peer-mesh" — direct WebSocket connections between daemons (recommended
 for permanent federations with stable hostnames). "relay" — daemons
 connect through a central relay server (simpler but requires a
 coordinator online).

Template: otzi-headless/listen
Type: string
Default: 0.0.0.0:8800
Description: Peer-mesh listen address (host:port)
 Address this node binds for inbound peer-mesh connections.

Template: otzi-headless/relay-url
Type: string
Description: Relay WebSocket URL
 Required when transport is "relay" — e.g. ws://relay.example:9000.

Template: otzi-headless/operator-bind
Type: string
Default: 127.0.0.1:7080
Description: Operator HTTP API bind (host:port)
 Local address the operator-facing HTTP API listens on. Default is
 loopback (recommended). For UDS or remote bind, edit
 /etc/otzi/daemon.toml after install.

Template: otzi-headless/node-id
Type: string
Description: Node identifier
 Logical name for this node (defaults to the system hostname). Used as
 [node].id in daemon.toml; must be unique across the ring.
